// DOM complement familial (L755-16/16-1, D755-6/6-1, R755-1..4).
//
// DEONTIC MAP: right-conferring rules (qualifying ages, small-family
// ceilings, open right, amounts, differential) plus three fund payment
// duties on the department track, plus the Title V broad track (statutory
// scope and available base/increased amounts, no duties). No recipient
// duties, powers, sanctions or deadlines in the 8-article scope:
// assessment runs through R. 532-1/R. 532-3 upstream, recovery through
// L. 553-2 (wave 5) — same finding as metropolitan CF. Duties are
// norm-conclusions (positions to observe), everything else a literal head.
// Evaluative channels: no organ judgment is named (channel 1 empty); the
// fund establishes the DOM frame, the young-child presence, the Title V
// frame and the stated figures (channel 2, case_input per package
// precedent); persons, dates, counts and the department class are direct
// case facts with provenance (channel 3).
//
// TERRITORY (D-76). R. 755-1 «dans les départements mentionnés à
// l'article L. 751-1» is department-only: award and differential rules
// require the provenance-bearing departement_l751_1(t) case fact besides
// the six-value guard, and conclude nothing for Saint-Barthélemy or
// Saint-Martin. L. 755-16/16-1 carry no local territorial phrase and sit
// under Title V; D. 755-6/6-1 rates are generic. The broad track states
// that Title V scope (six collectivities) and builds the two available
// amounts from the retained Title V frame without asserting R. 755-1 ages,
// ceilings, differential or duties for non-departments. The L. 751-1 list
// itself stays unowned (B-PFCF-DOM-TERRITOIRE).
//
// LIAISON (no duplication). Households with three or more children reuse
// the metropolitan R. 522-2/R. 522-4 machinery directly: the DOM award
// and amount rules read plafond_cf_applicable/plafond_majore_applicable,
// which already encode the tiered D-36 reading and the biactif/isole
// increment. Only one- and two-child households need new ceiling rules,
// because the metropolitan rules gate n >= 3. The biactif test
// (couple_biactif) and lone-parent fact (parent_isole) are household
// level and residence independent, so they are read, not redefined; the
// metropolitan §70 closures cover the `not` premises here as well.
//
// CEILINGS (D-83). R. 755-2 and R. 755-4 renvoi to R. 522-2 and R. 522-4,
// whose ceilings are the published DSS amounts (base, increments per child,
// two-earner increment; the increased amount has its own published base and
// increments): the DOM one- and two-child ceilings are built from the same
// facts as the metropolitan ones (03-plafond.law), so there is one source
// of figures. This closes Q-PFCF-1 for the DOM tracks as well: the
// two-earner increment of the increased amount is the published
// majoration_biactivite_majore.
//
// READINGS (adopted, recorded in lines/finish-dom-cf-owner.md):
// - R755-1 pins the vague L755-16 age limbs: every counted child is over
//   three (strict «plus de») and at least one is under five (strict
//   «moins de»); the L531-1 al. 1 renvoi carries no further executable
//   content once R755-1 governs.
// - «Tous âgés de plus de trois ans» is universal over counted children:
//   per-child cf_dom_enfant_ancien facts plus the count input contract
//   (metro B-PFCF-COMPTAGE pattern); «au moins l'un de moins de cinq ans»
//   is existential, established by the fund (presence_jeune_dom) under
//   the same contract with the per-child jeune facts.
// - L755-16-1 attributes the increased amount INSTEAD of the base amount
//   (metro D-39(a)): base rules require r > plafond_majore, majore rules
//   r <= plafond_majore.
// - R755-3 conditions the differential explicitly on R755-1, so the DOM
//   differential keeps the DOM frame/territory/young-child premises while
//   staying standalone from the open base right (no cf_dom_droit_ouvert
//   premise: the overrun household has none).
// - L755-16 al. 3 (CPI indexation) and L755-16-1 al. 2 (rates by decree,
//   substance in D755-6/6-1) carry no rule: despite with reason.
// - Mayotte and AUTRE conclude nothing anywhere; Saint-Barthélemy and
//   Saint-Martin conclude nothing on the R. 755-1 department track and
//   carry Title V scope plus available amounts only (B-PFCF-DOM-TERRITOIRE,
//   B-PFCF-DOM-TITRE-V). No SB/SM department fact and no R. 755-1 age gate
//   are invented for the broad track.
// - The retained Title V frame (cadre_cf_titre_v_remplie) qualifies the
//   collectivity award where non-department regulatory detail is genuinely
//   not pinned; available amounts are built from it, never «due», and bear
//   no duty. Base/majore exclusivity is not asserted there (ceilings stay
//   department-linked via R. 755-2/4).
//
// MONEY FORMS mirror 04-montant.law per track as retained package policy,
// not source-prescribed: no pinned CF/DOM text names cent-rounding or
// tie-breaking — D. 755-6 «Le montant … est fixé à 41,65 % …» and
// D. 755-6-1 «Le taux … est égal à 62,48 % …» give rates only.
// Base/majore round HALF_UP to the centime on both the department and the
// Title V broad track (adopted reading, SOURCE_PENDING; metropolitan
// precedent is not legal proof). The differential is exact (division
// refuses inexact quotients). Tests use exact non-tie amounts (166.60,
// 62.48, 133.28) and assert no tie-breaking, preserving non-tieability.
// Money x Decimal and Money / Decimal only; one- and two-child ceilings
// use literal counts, never Money x Integer.

language "law.core" version "0.2";
package fr.pf.cf version "0.1.0";
namespace "urn:fr:corpus:clir:pf-cf";

